---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const sessions = [
  {
    number: '01',
    question: 'Who',
    time: '12:00–1:00pm',
    title: 'Power goes to those who show up ready to do something',
    paragraphs: [
      'Canadian agrifood is shaped by people who grow food, build tools, and care for the systems around it. This is where we meet one another—not as an audience, but as people whose experience and imagination belong at the centre of the conversation.',
      'What do you see that others may be missing? What are you hoping to understand or change? Bring your perspective and questions. The day begins with the people who show up ready to do something.',
      'Across the landscape, the scarcest layer is often farmer agency: not access to a tool, but the ability to shape and benefit from it. This opening session asks what becomes possible when the people closest to the work have a meaningful role in shaping what comes next.',
    ],
    tone: 'moss',
  },
  {
    number: '02',
    question: 'What',
    time: '1:15–2:15pm',
    title: 'Intelligence begins on the farm and in the food',
    paragraphs: [
      'From farms and fields to processing and distribution, intelligence is taking on new forms. We will travel across the food system and meet people living with these changes.',
      'The examples are practical. They include OpenSprinkler irrigation, AquaCrop-OSPy crop-water modelling, UN FAO forest monitoring, CoopCycle logistics, and open diagnostic instruments. Together they show capacity being built across the food system, even when the pieces remain unevenly connected.',
      'Together, these examples open a larger question: how might Canadian agrifood gain the capacity to adapt and benefit from new intelligence without surrendering control of the systems that matter?',
    ],
    tone: 'ochre',
  },
  {
    number: '03',
    question: 'How',
    time: '2:30–3:30pm',
    title: 'The Future Is Something We Practise',
    paragraphs: [
      'A crisis moves through the food system, and the familiar ways of making decisions are no longer enough. The situation is fictional, but we can learn from the questions the scenario raises.',
      'What would you notice first? Who would you turn to? What would matter most? We will step into the moment together and consider how people and institutions might respond when the pressure is real.',
      'The landscape suggests that openness is layered. It may appear in a tool, a public standard, or a dataset, while the systems around them remain closed. The exercise turns that strategic question into a shared experience.',
    ],
    tone: 'pink',
  },
  {
    number: '04',
    question: 'When',
    time: '3:45–4:45pm',
    title: 'The Plot Thickens',
    paragraphs: [
      'After the speculation and discussion, we gather the threads. The day may have changed how we see the food system, the technologies moving through it, or the people trying to understand it.',
      'One finding stays with us: “The open agrifood layer has achieved robust, peer-reviewed, and production-proven viability across decentralized small-scale interventions, scientific simulation engines, and cooperative logistics, but hits a hard capital and biological wall at broad-acre industrial control.”',
      'What stayed with you? What new possibility appeared? What question became too interesting to leave behind? We will consider what a more capable and broadly beneficial agrifood future might require.',
    ],
    tone: 'blue',
  },
];
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero shell">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">A Future Herd spectacular event on AI and agrifood</p>
      <h1>Building the<br /><em>Open-Source</em> Future<br />of Canadian Agrifood</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">A half-day gathering for people who care about where food, intelligence, and collective possibility meet.</p>
      <p class="event-date">Thursday, October 29, 2026<br /><strong>12 noon–5:00pm</strong></p>
      <div class="event-meta">
        <span>Online</span><span>Discord</span><span>Half-day</span><span>Four sessions</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="orbit orbit-one"></div>
      <div class="orbit orbit-two"></div>
      <div class="orbit orbit-three"></div>
      <div class="sun"></div>
      <span class="art-note note-one">who</span>
      <span class="art-note note-two">what</span>
      <span class="art-note note-three">how</span>
      <span class="art-note note-four">when</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro shell">
    <div class="section-label">Why gather</div>
    <div class="intro-copy">
      <p class="intro-lede">Canadian agrifood is changing quickly. New forms of intelligence are moving through the food system, from the farm and the field to processing, distribution, retail, and the places where food is shared and eaten.</p>
      <p>Choices made now about knowledge, technology, and who gets to shape them will stay with us. This gathering brings together people working across Canadian agrifood and people trying to understand where it is going.</p>
      <p>We want to bring together the people whose knowledge and experience can help us understand what open-source AI means for Canadian agrifood.</p>
      <p>Here, “open” means that people can see enough of a tool or system to understand it, use it, adapt it, and sometimes share what they improve. That can build capacity and agency—but openness is not the same as ownership, control, or benefit. Those are the questions we want to explore.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="future-herd shell">
    <div class="section-label">The host</div>
    <div class="future-herd-copy">
      <h2>Meet the Future Herd</h2>
      <p>The Future Herd is a podcast and a growing conversation about the changes reshaping food and agriculture. It explores how collective wisdom and adaptive leadership can help us navigate a changing food system.</p>
      <p>That conversation brings together people with different experiences of the food system—people who work in it, study it, build for it, govern it, and care about where it is going. This event is one way the conversation becomes a shared experience rather than something we only encounter through a screen.</p>
      <p class="discord-note">The event will take place on the <strong>Future Herd Discord server</strong>: a shared online space where the gathering can happen, where participants can find one another, and where the conversation can continue beyond this day. <a href="https://thefutureherd.ca">Learn more about Future Herd</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="agenda shell" id="agenda">
    <div class="section-label">The day</div>
    <div class="agenda-head">
      <h2><span class="agenda-word">Who</span><span class="agenda-arrow">→</span><span class="agenda-word">What</span><span class="agenda-arrow">→</span><span class="agenda-word">How</span><span class="agenda-arrow">→</span><span class="agenda-word">When</span></h2>
      <p>Four ways of being together. One day to see what becomes possible. Each session is one hour, with a 15-minute break between sessions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="session-list">
      {sessions.map((session, index) => (
        <Fragment>
          {index > 0 && <div class="agenda-break">Break · {sessions[index - 1].time.split('–')[1]}–{session.time.split('–')[0]}</div>}
          <article class={`session session-${session.tone}`}>
          <div class="session-number">{session.number}</div>
          <div class="session-question">{session.question}</div>
          <div class="session-body">
            <p class="session-time">{session.time}</p>
            <h3>{session.title}</h3>
            {session.paragraphs.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
          </div>
          </article>
        </Fragment>
      ))}
      <article class="session session-wind-down">
        <div class="session-number">—</div>
        <div class="session-question">Wind down</div>
        <div class="session-body">
          <p class="session-time">4:45–5:00pm</p>
          <h3>Socialize and hang out</h3>
          <p>Stay with us after the event to socialize, hang out, and continue conversations informally.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="research-note shell">
    <div class="section-label">The research behind the gathering</div>
    <div class="research-copy">
      <p>This event grows from two connected projects. <strong>Open-Source Agrifood</strong>, from Future Herd, follows where openness, intelligence, and control are taking shape across the food system. It sits within Future Herd’s work in media, events, and organizing. <a href="/research">Read the accessible research overview</a>.</p>
      <p>The <a class="research-inline-link" href="https://agrifood.metaviews.ca"><strong>Agrifood AI Field Guide</strong></a>, from Metaviews, follows the development and application of AI across agrifood. It reflects Metaviews’ work in AI design and consulting, and brings together the people, technologies, and patterns that help us understand this changing field.</p>
      <p>The two projects run in parallel, with considerable overlap. Together they connect questions about AI, openness, capacity, and control—and invite us to consider what happens when AI agents participate in the work of discovering, connecting, and building tools for the food system.</p>
      <div class="research-links">
        <a href="/research">Open-Source Agrifood <span>Future Herd ↗</span></a>
        <a href="https://agrifood.metaviews.ca">Agrifood AI Field Guide <span>Metaviews ↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="invitation shell">
    <div class="section-label">Come as you are</div>
    <div class="invitation-copy">
      <h2>You do not need to be an expert.</h2>
      <p>Bring a question, an experience, a concern, a possibility—or simply a willingness to pay attention. Speak, listen, ask questions, share what you know, follow the conversation, or stay with it.</p>
      <p>Join us to explore the changing relationship between food, intelligence, and collective possibility in Canada.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .shell { max-width: 86rem; margin: 0 auto; padding-left: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 4rem); padding-right: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 4rem); }

  .hero {
    min-height: 42rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(18rem, 0.72fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding-top: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem);
    padding-bottom: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .eyebrow, .section-label {
    color: var(--ochre);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    line-height: 1.3;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1, h2, h3, p { margin-top: 0; }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400; }

  h1 {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(3.35rem, 7.2vw, 7.2rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    line-height: 0.93;
  }

  h1 em { color: var(--moss); font-style: normal; }
  .hero-lede { max-width: 30rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.8vw, 1.45rem); line-height: 1.4; }
  .event-date { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; color: var(--moss-dark); font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.35rem; line-height: 1.15; }
  .event-date strong { color: var(--ochre); font-weight: 400; }

  .event-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.55rem 1.25rem; margin-top: 2rem; color: var(--ink-faint); font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .event-meta span::before { content: '·'; margin-right: 0.5rem; color: var(--ochre); }
  .event-meta span:first-child::before { content: ''; margin: 0; }

  .hero-art { position: relative; min-height: 28rem; }
  .sun { position: absolute; width: clamp(8rem, 18vw, 15rem); aspect-ratio: 1; top: 28%; left: 31%; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--ochre); box-shadow: 1.5rem 1.5rem 0 var(--pink); }
  .orbit { position: absolute; border: 1px solid var(--moss); border-radius: 50%; transform: rotate(-28deg); }
  .orbit-one { width: 92%; height: 40%; top: 32%; left: 4%; }
  .orbit-two { width: 74%; height: 82%; top: 8%; left: 14%; transform: rotate(54deg); }
  .orbit-three { width: 38%; height: 104%; top: -2%; left: 34%; transform: rotate(22deg); border-color: var(--ochre); }
  .art-note { position: absolute; color: var(--moss-dark); font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.2rem; font-style: italic; }
  .note-one { top: 18%; left: 13%; }
  .note-two { top: 68%; right: 5%; }
  .note-three { bottom: 3%; left: 39%; }
  .note-four { top: 7%; right: 24%; }

  .intro, .agenda, .invitation { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 0.28fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 7rem; }
  .intro-copy { max-width: 48rem; font-size: 1.16rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .intro-lede { color: var(--moss-dark); font-family: var(--display); font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.55rem); line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
  .future-herd { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 0.28fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 7rem; }
  .future-herd-copy { max-width: 50rem; font-size: 1.16rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .future-herd-copy h2 { margin-bottom: 1rem; color: var(--moss-dark); font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 4rem); letter-spacing: -0.06em; line-height: 0.98; }
  .future-herd-copy p { max-width: 46rem; }
  .discord-note { margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--moss-dark); font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.25; }
  .discord-note a { color: var(--ochre); text-decoration: none; }
  .discord-note a:hover { color: var(--moss); }
  .agenda { display: block; }
  .agenda-head { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; margin: 1rem 0 3rem 20%; }
  .agenda-head h2 { margin-bottom: 0; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 5rem); letter-spacing: -0.06em; line-height: 0.98; }
  .agenda-head h2 .agenda-word { color: var(--moss-dark); font-family: var(--body); font-size: 1em; font-weight: 650; vertical-align: baseline; }
  .agenda-head h2 .agenda-arrow { color: var(--ochre); font-family: var(--body); font-size: 0.5em; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0.16em; vertical-align: 0.15em; }
  .agenda-head p { max-width: 14rem; margin-bottom: 0.2rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .session-list { margin-left: 20%; }
  .session { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4rem 7rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1rem; padding: 1.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .session:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .agenda-break { margin: 0.75rem 0; color: var(--ink-faint); font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .agenda-closing { margin: 1rem 0 0 20%; color: var(--moss-dark); font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .session-number { color: var(--ink-faint); font-size: 0.75rem; padding-top: 0.3rem; }
  .session-question { color: var(--moss); font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.35rem; font-style: italic; padding-top: 0.1rem; }
  .session-time { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; color: var(--ochre); font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 750; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .session-body h3 { max-width: 34rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.65rem); letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1.02; }
  .session-body p { max-width: 42rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1rem; }
  .session-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .session-body p:nth-of-type(3) { color: var(--moss); font-family: var(--display); font-size: 1.08rem; font-style: italic; }
  .session-ochre .session-question { color: var(--ochre); }
  .session-pink .session-question { color: #a56462; }
  .session-blue .session-question { color: #5f6d91; }
  .session-wind-down { background: rgba(219, 169, 160, 0.12); padding-left: 1rem; padding-right: 1rem; }

  .invitation { background: var(--moss-dark); color: var(--paper); border-top: 0; padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 5rem; }
  .invitation .section-label { color: var(--pink); }
  .invitation-copy { max-width: 49rem; }
  .invitation h2 { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; color: var(--paper); font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 5rem); letter-spacing: -0.06em; line-height: 0.98; }
  .invitation p { max-width: 42rem; color: rgba(244, 240, 231, 0.8); font-size: 1.15rem; }

  .research-note { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 0.28fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 6rem; }
  .research-copy { max-width: 52rem; }
  .research-copy > p { max-width: 44rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-family: var(--display); font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.4vw, 2.1rem); line-height: 1.15; }
  .research-inline-link { color: var(--moss); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--ochre); text-underline-offset: 0.16em; }
  .research-inline-link:hover { color: var(--ochre); }
  .research-links { display: grid; gap: 0.7rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .research-links a { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: 0.8rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--moss-dark); font-size: 0.95rem; text-decoration: none; }
  .research-links a:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .research-links a:hover { color: var(--ochre); }
  .research-links span { color: var(--ink-faint); font-size: 0.85rem; }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; min-height: auto; }
    .hero-art { min-height: 21rem; max-width: 32rem; width: 100%; margin: 0 auto; }
    .intro, .future-herd, .research-note, .invitation { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
    .agenda-head { margin-left: 0; display: block; }
    .agenda-head p { margin-top: 1rem; }
    .session-list { margin-left: 0; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .hero { padding-top: 3.5rem; }
    h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 15vw, 5rem); }
    .hero-art { min-height: 17rem; }
    .intro, .agenda, .invitation { padding-bottom: 4rem; }
    .session { grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr; gap: 0.6rem 1rem; }
    .session-number { grid-row: span 2; }
    .session-question { grid-column: 2; }
    .session-body { grid-column: 2; }
    .session-body h3 { font-size: 2rem; }
  }
</style>
